    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "SwCNQ",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7354,
      "name": "30 · STATE / EDGE-CASE INDEX",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 64,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "m8qe6",
          "name": "Zone label",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
          "content": "30 · STATE / EDGE-CASE INDEX",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-page-title",
          "fontWeight": "bold"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Qfll0",
          "name": "States drawn, and the one that is not",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "RgbNJ",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "States drawn, and the one that is not",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "snlRs",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "J11.A / 01 · Appearance is drawn at all four sizes, because the shell differs at all four and Settings is the first screen in the product reached from the Settings destination.\n\nJ11.B / 01 · On a touch screen is drawn at Compact only. The rule is about pointer capability and not about width, so it applies at every size; Compact is where a coarse pointer is overwhelmingly likely and drawing it four times would say the opposite.\n\nNot drawn: a saving state, because nothing is saved; a validation error, because neither control can be wrong; and an empty state, because a screen of settings is never empty.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "eolMa",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8153,
      "name": "40 · THEME + ACCESSIBILITY QA",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 64,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lZwbq",
          "name": "Zone label",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
          "content": "40 · THEME + ACCESSIBILITY QA",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-page-title",
          "fontWeight": "bold"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "bO5QM",
          "name": "Theme and accessibility QA",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X5WqWz",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "Theme and accessibility QA",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hl4yq",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Both controls are Segmented control instances, so their contrast, focus ring and 44 px target floor are already asserted in the library's own QA zone and are not re-asserted here.\n\nWhat is specific to this screen and cannot be drawn: the choice has to be in force before first paint, and the announcement when it changes. Both are contracts in the change's canvas record.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "fSEVL",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8912,
      "name": "90 · TEMPORARY NOTES",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 64,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RYRic",
          "name": "Zone label",
          "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
          "content": "90 · TEMPORARY NOTES",
          "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
          "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-page-title",
          "fontWeight": "bold"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "zXljb",
          "name": "One section, and when the list card arrives",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LFPCj",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "One section, and when the list card arrives",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zRPmw",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Settings holds one section today. ADR 0005 chooses the form by the content and only by the content: a longer or growing set of subdivisions becomes a list card in the page, and a fixed handful of peer views becomes tabs. One section is neither, so neither is drawn.\n\nThe library's Settings templates draw the list card with six rows — Profile, Connections, Categories, Rules, Notifications, Export — and the templates' own contract table marks those as provisional rather than decided. Drawing them here would turn an illustration into a promise.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "beBmG",
          "name": "Where the sharing surface will go",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pbLxq",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "Where the sharing surface will go",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "EMxm7",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "ADR 0019 named a sharing surface that spans banks, so a member can answer \"what can my partner see?\" without opening every bank in turn, and deliberately left it out. This change adds the screen that would hold it and does not add it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
